Markers, you mean?

How many you get from non-wish sources is highly variable
due to being heavily dependent on bones.  Several roles
start (or have a chance to start) with a magic marker, so
early bones piles often have one.  I've seen bones levels
with more than one marker (when more than one player died
there).  Of course, how many bones levels you get varies
quite a bit.  In some games you don't see any markers unless
you wish for them, because all the bones you run into in the
early game are roles that don't get them, and in the middle
game a lot of players have either used their markers or
stashed them.

The largest number of markers I've ever had was in a game
where smoky potions were full healing.  After I had acquired
everything else I wanted to wish for, I still had potions,
which I wanted to quaff anyway for the max HP, and I ended
up getting several more markers as a result.  Magic markers
are my standard default wish, when I don't particularly need
anything else.  (This is generally a late-game phenomenon,
of course; in the early and middle game there are usually
still other things I need, in which case I'd only wish for a
marker if I had a specific need for it that outweighed the
other items on my wish list.)


